WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Select Figure 8 to see the original figure beside its explanation.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Open panel A for a closer look.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Click the horizontal axis. The exaggeration factor ρ controls attraction between neighbours in t-SNE.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.000
Panel A is now in the slide basket. Add a speaking note below the figure.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.000
Add panel B and note which part of the axis you want to compare.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Drag panel B ahead of panel A.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Read the central scientific question, then follow its background and aims.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:37.000
Choose Current figure to find the branch for Figure 8, shown on the right.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Open Slides, select a panel and edit the text on the slide.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:50.000
Write what you plan to say in the separate speaker notes field.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:54.000
Start rehearsing with just the slide on screen.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.000
Choose Show notes to reveal your speaking notes.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Return to Slides and export the PowerPoint with its speaker notes.
